  "article": [
    {
      "level": 3,
      "heading": "Discussion",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "Apps that use the Advanced Commerce API manage their own catalogs of in-app purchases. You assign a SKU to each product, along with other information such as the display name, description, and price.",
          "refs": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The SKU value isn’t displayed to customers, and isn’t stored by App Store Connect.",
          "refs": []
        },
        {
          "text": "A SKU can represent any type of in-app purchase product that your app offers, including products with a one-time charge, auto-renewable subscriptions, or bundles and items in subscriptions.",
          "refs": []
        }
      ],
